{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he dwelt</b> This is what the verse says: 'YHWH has removed your judgments, has cleared your enemies.' Parable of a field that was harvested and winnowed: one separates the straw and the chaff and discards them, and the grain remains in its place. As written of Esau: 'and he went to the land of,' but of Jacob it is written: 'and Jacob dwelt.'" "<b>מגורי</b> Two times in the Masorah: here and the other מגורי אל חרב. Even though he had 'fear of the sword,' he dwelt among them. Parable of one who saw a pack of dogs that wanted to bite him, and he sat among them. Thus Jacob dwelt among Esau and his chieftains." "<b>מגורי אביו</b> in gematria is חברון." "<b>וישב יעקב בארץ מגורי אביו</b> in gematria is 'he dwelt to fulfill the commandment of honoring.' In the reward of honor, Esau merited all this honor." "<b>מגורי</b> The yud is bent like a kaf. He said: That Esau merited all this honor was in the reward of the honor. And even though my father blessed me with ten blessings, I needed to send ten things, as written: 'two hundred goats, etc.' I will go and humble myself and honor my father in Hebron."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:51.442594826Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}